<article class="env-definition" id="0249">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0249">Definition <span data-tag="0249">85.27.1</span>.</a> Let $a : Y \to X$ be a morphism of simplicial schemes. We say $a$ is <em>cartesian</em>, or that <em>$Y$ is cartesian over $X$</em>, if for every morphism $\varphi : [n] \to [m]$ of $\Delta $ the corresponding diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Y_ m \ar[r]_ a \ar[d]_{Y(\varphi )} &  X_ m \ar[d]^{X(\varphi )}\\  Y_ n \ar[r]^{a} &  X_ n }  \]
</div>
  <p> is a fibre square in the category of schemes. </p>
</article>